          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Two clarifications that prevent expensive mistakes. First, series products are not fake — they are legitimate baijiu from the same corporate group, made to different specifications and sold at different prices. Second, they are not the flagship, and no amount of brand association changes what is in the bottle. If you are buying a gift, buy the product you can name exactly.</p>
      <div class="callout warning"><strong>On the corporate family:</strong> the Moutai group's holdings have changed over the years, and some brands once associated with it are now independent. Do not assume that a bottle bearing a related name is produced by the same company as Flying Fairy — check the producer (生产商) line on the back label.</div>

      <h2 id="versus">Moutai versus other sauce aroma</h2>
      <p>Moutai is the benchmark, not the only option. Two competitors are worth knowing, and both are better value for anyone who wants to drink rather than display.</p>
